Forgejo on FenrirOS
===================

Installed inert: the service is not enabled, there is no configuration and
no account.

Setup:

    1. Write /etc/forgejo/app.ini (owner root:forgejo). Start from only:

           [server]
           HTTP_ADDR = 127.0.0.1
           HTTP_PORT = 3000
           [database]
           DB_TYPE = sqlite3
           PATH = /var/lib/forgejo/data/forgejo.db
           [repository]
           ROOT = /var/lib/forgejo/repositories

       (the service user must be able to write it for the install page to
       save the settings: chmod g+w, or write the file yourself and set
       INSTALL_LOCK = true plus the secrets.)
    2. dinitctl enable forgejo
    3. Open http://127.0.0.1:3000 and complete the install page (it creates
       the administrator). Until INSTALL_LOCK = true the install page is open
       to whoever reaches the port first: bind to localhost, or do this at
       once, on a trusted network.

The service runs as the forgejo user (home /var/lib/forgejo). For SSH access
(git clone forgejo@host:...) the SSH server must allow that user, or set
[server] START_SSH_SERVER = true and SSH_PORT.

Gitea (package gitea) can be installed next to it; they share nothing
(own binary, user, directories). Do not point both at the same data or
database, and give them different HTTP_PORT values.
